          "accessed": "2026-11-03",
          "tier": 4,
          "license": "CC0"
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "Above them is a poem written by a Japanese Buddhist monk. The poem turns on the image of the monk’s black hair being cut when he entered the priesthood, comparing it to the color of lily seeds. In the print, cotton seeds take their place.",
